<title>GERMANY: Pan-German Jan adjusted jobless up 160,000.</title>
<headline>Pan-German Jan adjusted jobless up 160,000.</headline>
<dateline>NUREMBERG, Germany 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Labour Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> PAN-GERMAN UNEMPLOYMENT   Jan 97	Dec 96	   Jan 96</p>
<p> Number (unadj)		4.658 million   4.148 million	4.159 million</p>
<p> Number (adj)		  4.317 million   4.157 million	3.858 million</p>
<p> Change in adj number	+160,000    +45,000	  +56,000</p>
<p> Rate (unadj)		  12.2 pct    10.8 pct	 10.8 pct</p>
<p> Short-time workers	  292,631     204,760	  293,949</p>
<p> Vacancies (unadj)	   297,198     270,890	  296,147</p>
<p> Change in numbers in work Nov 96	Oct 96</p>
<p>				  -61,000	-44,000</p>
<p>NOTE - Numbers in work data refer to change from previous month. Details on numbers in work to be released later today.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom 49 228 26097150</p>
</text>
